WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:05.910
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:13.590
The reading from the Sinaxadion for July 12 on which we commemorate our righteous father

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.600
Biasios the Athenite.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:26.840
On July 25 in the year 1924, the future elder Biasios was born to pious parents in the town

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.960
of Farrassa, Cappadocia, of Asia Minor.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:39.120
The family's spiritual father, the priest monk Arsenios, the now canonized Saint Arsenios

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:46.400
of Cappadocia, baptized the babe with his own name, prophesying his future profession

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.320
as a monk.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:55.560
A week after the baptism and barely a month after his birth, Arsenios was driven along with

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.440
his family out of Asia Minor by the Turks.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:07.360
Saint Arsenios guided his flock along their 400-mile track to Greece.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:14.480
After a number of stops along the way, Arsenios' family finally ended up in the town of

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.480
Conezzen Epidos.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:24.800
Saint Arsenios had reposed as he had prophesied 40 days after their establishment in Greece,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.960
and he left as his spiritual heir, the infant Arsenios.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:37.440
The young Arsenios was wholly given over to God and spent his free time in the silence

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.440
of nature, where he would pray for hours on end.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:48.480
Having completed his elementary education, he learned the trade of carpentry.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.080
He worked as a carpenter until his mandatory military service.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:02:00.000
He served in the army during the dangerous days of the end of World War II.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.240
Arsenios was brave and self-sacrificing, always desiring to put his own life at risk, so as

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.920
to spare his brother.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:15.960
He was particularly concerned about his fellow soldiers who had left wives and children

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.360
to serve.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:25.360
Having completed his obligation to his country, Arsenios received his discharge in 1949, and

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.120
greatly desired to begin his monastic life on the Holy Mountain.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:37.600
Before being able to settle there, however, he had to fulfill his responsibility to his family,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.720
to look after his sisters, who were as yet unmarried.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:48.160
Having provided for his sister's future, he was free to begin his monastic vocation

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.160
with the clean conscience.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:59.360
In 1950 he arrived on Mount Athos, where he learned his first lessons in the monastic way

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:07.680
from the virtuous ascetic Father Kiddil, the future abbot of Kutlumusio monastery.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.880
But he was unable to stay at his side as he had hoped, and so was sent to the monastery

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.880
of Esfigmenu.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:23.440
He was a novice there for four years, after which he was transferred a monk in 1954, with

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.840
the name of Erkios.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:33.600
He was a conscientious monk, finding ways to both complete his obedience, which required contact

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:40.720
with others, and to preserve his silence, so as to progress in the art of prayer.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:47.280
He was always selfless in helping his brethren, unwilling to rest while others worked, though

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:53.760
he may have already completed his own obedience, as he loved his brothers greatly and without

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.160
distinction.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:02.280
In addition to his ascetic struggles and the common life in the monastery, he was spiritually

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.680
enriched through the reading of soul-propheting books.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:14.160
In particular, he read the lives of the saints, the Yerantikon, and especially the ascetical

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:19.040
homelies of St. Isaac the Syrian.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:26.880
Soon after his tonsure, monk Abirkios left Esfigmenu and joined the then-irrorithmic brotherhood

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.800
of Philotheum monastery, where his uncle was a monk.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:38.600
He put himself under obedience to the virtuous Elder Simeon, who gave him the small schema

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:44.960
in 1956, with the new name Baesios.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:52.200
Father Baesios dwelt deeply on the thought that his own spiritual failures and lack of love

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:58.840
were the cause of his neighbor's shortcomings, as well as of the world's ills.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:05.840
He harshly accused himself, pushing himself to greater self-denial, and more fervent prayer

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:09.360
for his soul and for the whole world.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:16.720
Furthermore, he cultivated the habit of always seeking the good reason for a potentially scandalous

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:24.520
event and for people's actions, and in this way he preserved himself from judging others.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:30.840
For example, pilgrims to mount Athos had been scandalized by the strange behavior and

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:38.920
stories told by a certain monk, and when they met Elder Baesios, they asked him what was

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.520
wrong with the monk.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:48.800
He warned them not to judge others, and that this monk was actually virtuous and was simply

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:56.720
pretending to be a fool when visitors would come, so as to preserve his silence.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:04.240
In 1958, Elder Baesios was asked to spend some time in and around his home village of

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:11.760
Gonitsa, so as to support the faithful against the proselytism of Protestant groups.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:17.200
He greatly encouraged the faithful there, helping many people.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:25.080
Afterwards, in 1962, he left to visit Sinai, where he stayed for two years.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:31.800
During this time, he became beloved of the Bedouins, who benefited both spiritually as well

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.120
as materially from his presence.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:41.520
The Elder used the money he received from the sale of his carved wooden handicrafts to

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.360
buy them food.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:53.400
On his return to mount Athos in 1964, Elder Baesios took up residence at the Skiti of Ividon

00:06:53.400 --> 00:07:00.960
before moving to Katunakia at the southernmost tip of Mount Athos, for a short stay in the

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.880
desert there.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:08.040
The Elder's failing health may have been part of the reason for his departure from the

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.560
desert.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:16.200
In 1966, he was operated on, and had part of his lungs removed.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.600
It was during this time of hospitalization that his long friendship with the then young

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:31.680
sisterhood of St. John the Theologian in Surati, just outside of Thessaloniki, began.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:37.320
During his operation, he greatly needed blood, and it was then that a group of novices,

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:42.480
from the monastery, donated blood to save him.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:49.320
Elder Baesios was most grateful, and after his recovery did whatever he could, materially

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:54.520
and spiritually, to help them build their monastery.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:08:02.280
In 1968, he spent time at the monastery of Stavronikita, helping with its spiritual, as well

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:05.760
as material, renovation.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:12.200
While there, he had the blessing of being in contact with the ascetic Elder Tykon, who

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:18.520
lived in the hermitage of the Holy Cross near Stavronikita.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:27.920
Elder Baesios stayed by his side until his repose, serving himselflessly as his disciple.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:34.800
It was during this time that Elder Tykon clothed Father Baesios in the great schema.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:41.320
According to the wishes of the Elder, Father Baesios remained in his hermitage after his

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.000
repose.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:50.800
He stayed there until 1979, when he moved on to his final home on the Holy Mountain,

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:58.000
the hermitage of Panaguda, which belongs to the monastery of Kotlin Musil.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:05.080
It was here at Panaguda that Elder Baesios' fame, as a god-bearing elder, grew, drawing

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.560
to him the sick and suffering people of God.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:17.440
He received them all day long, dedicating the night to God in prayer, visual, and spiritual

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.840
struggle.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:25.220
His regime of prayer and asceticism, with which he served God and his fellow-man, his

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:32.400
strictness with himself, the austerity of his regime, and his sensitive nature, made him

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.200
increasingly prone to sickness.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.480
In addition to respiratory problems, in his later days he suffered from a serious

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:46.160
hernia that made life very painful.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:53.160
When he was forced to leave the Holy Mountain for various reasons, often due to his illness,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:10:00.760
he would receive pilgrims for hours on end at the women's monastery at Surat-i and the

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:07.500
physical effort which this entailed in his weakened state caused him such pain that he

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.160
would turn pale.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:16.400
He bore his suffering with much grace, however, confident that, as God knows what is best

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:20.760
for us, it could not be otherwise.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:28.360
He would say that God is greatly touched when someone who is in great suffering does not complain,

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:33.480
but rather uses his energy to pray for others.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:40.040
In addition to his other illness, he suffered from hemorrhaging which left him very weak.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:46.520
In his final weeks before leaving the Holy Mountain, he would often fall unconscious.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:54.520
On the 5th of October in 1993, the elder left his beloved Holy Mountain for the last

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.400
time.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:03.040
Although he had planned on being off the mountain for just a few days, while in Thessaloniki he

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:09.160
was diagnosed with cancer that needed immediate treatment.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:14.560
After the operation he spent some time recovering in the hospital and was then transferred to

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:18.320
the monastery at Surat-i.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:26.800
Despite his critical state, he received people listening to their sorrow and counseling them.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:33.880
After his operation, elder Paesios had his heart set on returning to Mount Athos.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:39.480
His attempts to do so, however, were hindered by his failing health.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:46.280
His last days were full of suffering, but also of the joy of the martyrs.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:53.480
On July 11, 1994, he received Holy Communion for the last time.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:59.720
The next day, elder Paesios gave his soul into God's keeping.

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:07.640
He was buried according to his wishes at the monastery of St. John the Theologian in Surat-i.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:13.800
Elder Paesios, perhaps more than any other contemporary elder, has captured the minds

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:17.160
and hearts of Greek people.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:23.520
Many books of his councils have been published, and the monastery at Surat-i has undertaken

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:31.560
a great work, organizing the elder's writings and councils into impressive volumes, benefiting

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.920
his memory.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:41.200
Thousands of pilgrims visit his grave each year, so as to receive his blessing.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:47.680
Elder Paesios, the Athenite, was glorified as a saint by the Holy Synod of the Patriarchate

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:54.960
of Constantinople on January 13, 2015.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:13:01.160
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.160
and save us.
